In this Folder, I am posting the things about Postgre SQL practice from Book Practical SQL.
Lessons I have learned
a) How we can make Table and Insert Values in Database.
b) DataTypes 
c) Select Statement, Where, Order by, operator(=,<,>), OR and AND operator, LIKE (Case Sensitive),ILIKE ( Not Case Sensitive).
d) Data Types
  i) Text, Numeric, and Date Time
  ii) Text - char(n), varchar(n), and Text
      char(n) - fixed space allocated by n and fixed character should be put based on n.
      varchar(n) - variable space allocated by number of character you put and the length is fixed by n.
      text - unlimited charcter can be put
  iii) Numeric - Integers and Decimal
       Integers - smallint, integers,bigint
       Auto Increment Integers - smallserial,serial,bigserial
  iv) Decimal - Fixed and Floating
  v) Dates and Time - TimeStamp (Date and Time), dates - (date only), time (time only) and interval (days)
  v) JSON and JSON B 
      JSON - Put the data on keys and pairs. Example
        {
          'Name' : 'Anush',
          'Address' : 'Melbourne'
        }
      JSONB put the above value in binary format which helps sorting the data fastly.
  vi) Casting - converting one type of data types into another using CAST() or :: (name :: text) 
e) Importing and Exporting
  i) Creating table and Copying the data with the help of COPY table name FROM path director with (FORMAT CSV, DELIMITER)
  ii) Copying data with sub coulmns only
  iii) Exporting Table with Help of COPY table name to path director with (FORMAT CSV, DELIMITER)
  iv) Only Exporting sub columns
f) Basic Math and Statistics in SQL
  We can perform basics maths like addition, subtraction, multiplication, 
  and division. We can also do modulus, exponent, sqaure root and cube root.
  We can perform this column of numeric data types.
  Order of Mathemathics
  - Exponent
  - Division
  - Multiplication
  - Addition 
  -Subtraction
  We just need to know SQL follow BODMAS Rule.
  B for Brackets
  O - OF ( Not Used in SQL)
  D - Division
  M - Multiplication
  A - Addition
  S - Subtraction
  We can use this mathematical operations in numeric column of SQL.
  We can use mean, median and mode in SQL.
  for mean - we have avg ()
  for mode - we have mode ()
  But for median, 1st Quartile and 3rd Quartile, we have percentile_cont
  syntax
  percentile_cont(0.5) - for median
  with in (order by column)
  LikeWise 0.25 - for 1st Quartile, and 0.75 for 3rd Quartile
g) Joining Table
    Types of Join
    Join - return rows from both table where mathcing values are found
    Left Join - return every row from left table and show mathcing value of right table
    Right Join - return every row from right table and show matching value of left table
    FULL outer Join - returns every value from both table and joins the value where the value matched
    CROSS Join - returns every possible combination from both tables
    Relation ship between table
    One to One Relationship - One table of  row match with only one row of other table
    Example: State Population of Australia and State Income of Australia - We can have only 7 row in total if we join
    One to Many Relationship - One row of table match with many row of other table
    Example: One state of Australia has many cities and suburbs.
    Many to Many Relation - one table can relate to multiple items in another table and vice versa
    Example: one state can many laws and one law can implement in many state
